.TH VRCONTROLLER 1 "2026-10-12" "vrcontroller 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vrcontroller \- use a Samsung Gear VR Controller as mouse and keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrcontroller
.RB [ run | pair ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-mac
.IR address ]
.RB [ \-\-status\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vrcontroller run
(the default) connects to a paired Gear VR Controller over Bluetooth Low Energy and
replays its touchpad and buttons as a virtual input device through
.IR /dev/uinput .
When no controller is paired it pairs the first one that advertises (see
.B auto_pair
below), and it pairs again when the controller has forgotten the pairing.
It normally runs as the systemd user unit
.BR vrcontroller.service ,
started with the graphical session.
.PP
.B vrcontroller pair
forgets any existing pairing of a Gear VR Controller and pairs the one that is in pairing
mode (hold home until the LED blinks).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Configuration file (default:
.IR ~/.config/vrcontroller/config.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-mac " address"
Use this controller instead of looking up the first paired one.
.TP
.BI \-\-status\-port " port"
Port of the local status page on 127.0.0.1 (default 8765, 0 disables it).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
For
.BR pair :
how long to wait for the controller (default 60).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vrcontroller/config.toml
Mapping, pointer and scroll settings, and
.BR auto_pair .
All keys are documented in
.IR /usr/share/doc/vrcontroller/examples/config.example.toml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/vrcontroller/README.md
